   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 7: Redes Neuronales desde Cero\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** Una red neuronal aprende patrones complejos ajustando pesos mediante backpropagation. Cada neurona calcula: `output = activation(weights @ input + bias)`.\n", "\n", "**Backpropagation:** Calcula el gradiente de la loss respecto a cada peso, usando la chain rule. El optimizador (SGD, Adam) actualiza los pesos en dirección opuesta al gradiente."],
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import numpy as np\n", "\n", "# Red neuronal desde cero (sin frameworks)\n", "class NeuralNet:\n", "    def __init__(self, input_size, hidden_size, output_size, lr=0.01):\n", "        self.W1 = np.random.randn(input_size, hidden_size) * 0.01\n", "        self.b1 = np.zeros((1, hidden_size))\n", "        self.W2 = np.random.randn(hidden_size, output_size) * 0.01\n", "        self.b2 = np.zeros((1, output_size))\n", "        self.lr = lr\n", "\n", "    def relu(self, x):\n", "        return np.maximum(0, x)\n", "\n", "    def sigmoid(self, x):\n", "        return 1 / (1 + np.exp(-np.clip(x, -500, 500)))\n", "\n", "    def forward(self, X):\n", "        self.z1 = X @ self.W1 + self.b1\n", "        self.a1 = self.relu(self.z1)\n", "        self.z2 = self.a1 @ self.W2 + self.b2\n", "        self.a2 = self.sigmoid(self.z2)\n", "        return self.a2\n", "\n", "    def backward(self, X, y):\n", "        m = X.shape[0]\n", "        dz2 = self.a2 - y\n", "        dW2 = (self.a1.T @ dz2) / m\n", "        db2 = np.sum(dz2, axis=0, keepdims=True) / m\n", "        da1 = dz2 @ self.W2.T\n", "        dz1 = da1 * (self.z1 > 0)\n", "        dW1 = (X.T @ dz1) / m\n", "        db1 = np.sum(dz1, axis=0, keepdims=True) / m\n", "        self.W1 -= self.lr * dW1\n", "        self.b1 -= self.lr * db1\n", "        self.W2 -= self.lr * dW2\n", "        self.b2 -= self.lr * db2\n", "\n", "    def loss(self, y_true, y_pred):\n", "        return -np.mean(y_true * np.log(y_pred + 1e-8) + (1-y_true) * np.log(1-y_pred + 1e-8))\n", "\n", "# EJERCICIO 7: Entrena la red en make_classification data\n", "# a) Inicializa la red\n", "# b) Entrena 1000 epochs\n", "# c) Grafica la loss curve\n", "# d) Evalúa accuracy en test set\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
